{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 3336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "BuzzFeed and VICE were the digital media\nunicorns of the 2010s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3336,
    "dDurationMs": 1377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this fast emerging era"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4713,
    "dDurationMs": 3628,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of social media, smartphones, and video,\nthese two companies had seemingly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8341,
    "dDurationMs": 1377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "figured out the secret sauce"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9718,
    "dDurationMs": 2377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on how to go viral in \nthis new online world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12095,
    "dDurationMs": 1209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were fast, nimble,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13304,
    "dDurationMs": 4171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and hungry - free from the bureaucracy,\neditorial norms, and newsroom traditions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17475,
    "dDurationMs": 1001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of legacy media."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18476,
    "dDurationMs": 1335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They covered taboo topics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19811,
    "dDurationMs": 1668,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wrote for relatability rather than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21479,
    "dDurationMs": 3629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prescription, published without paywalls\nor regwalls, and reinvented"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25108,
    "dDurationMs": 3754,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "content from static text\ninto dynamic, interactive social pieces."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28903,
    "dDurationMs": 1627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was free content delivered at an"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30530,
    "dDurationMs": 2878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unprecedented pace, volume, \nquality, and swagger"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33408,
    "dDurationMs": 2753,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and their regular virality\nfueled organic distribution"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36161,
    "dDurationMs": 1334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to millions around the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37495,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Backed by flourishing viewership,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38955,
    "dDurationMs": 1794,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "BuzzFeed and VICE fundraised their way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40749,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to multi-billion dollar valuations,\nusing the investment to elevate production"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44669,
    "dDurationMs": 3045,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "value, expand genres,\nand build newsrooms of their own."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47797,
    "dDurationMs": 2253,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As these startups\nexpanded into journalism,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50050,
    "dDurationMs": 3753,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the line that once divided legacy\nmedia and digital media vanished."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53803,
    "dDurationMs": 2336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "BuzzFeed and VICE\nsoon started collecting Emmys and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56139,
    "dDurationMs": 1168,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pulitzers for their work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57307,
    "dDurationMs": 1293,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The viewership quality and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58600,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "virality was visible, and it wasn't hard\nfor the public and venture"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61561,
    "dDurationMs": 2085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "capitalists to imagine \nthat BuzzFeed and VICE"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63646,
    "dDurationMs": 2837,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had become for millennials\nwhat The New York Times and CNN"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66483,
    "dDurationMs": 3169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were for boomers. Brands and advertisers\nwho were eager to sell"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69652,
    "dDurationMs": 3879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to this new generation began diverting\nspend away from these legacy publications"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73740,
    "dDurationMs": 2502,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and towards these red-hot digital\nmedia startups."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76242,
    "dDurationMs": 1585,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "VICE and BuzzFeed led the way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77827,
    "dDurationMs": 2127,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there were also smaller \nstartups like VOX,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79954,
    "dDurationMs": 1043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thrillist, and Business"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80997,
    "dDurationMs": 2211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Insider who surged off these\nsame tailwinds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83208,
    "dDurationMs": 2544,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everyone assumed that the business\nwould take care of itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85752,
    "dDurationMs": 2461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No one had ever had this many eyeballs\nbefore, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88213,
    "dDurationMs": 2252,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with so many impressions\nto sell to advertisers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90465,
    "dDurationMs": 3837,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profit would simply be a matter of when\nand not if. Their founders proclaimed that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94302,
    "dDurationMs": 2127,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they were trailblazers\nwith no comparables."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96429,
    "dDurationMs": 2086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They had none of the overhead of legacy\nmedia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98515,
    "dDurationMs": 2002,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There were no printing presses\nand they didn't have to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100517,
    "dDurationMs": 2085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physically throw their content\nin front of people's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102602,
    "dDurationMs": 2169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doorsteps every day\njust to get readers and best"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104771,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of all, they didn't have any aging,\nunionized workforces."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107732,
    "dDurationMs": 3170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They asserted that digital media\nwas a new type of business with its own"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110902,
    "dDurationMs": 1043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fundamentals, where all the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111945,
    "dDurationMs": 3628,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consumption, distribution, and creation\nwould be entirely online."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115657,
    "dDurationMs": 1501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Media tycoons like Disney's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117158,
    "dDurationMs": 2586,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bob Iger and Fox's Rupert\nMurdoch had all heard the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119744,
    "dDurationMs": 2294,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tales from Silicon Valley\nabout disruption."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122038,
    "dDurationMs": 834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The news had served"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122872,
    "dDurationMs": 2419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the foundation to their business \nempires, and the risk"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125291,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of extinction in a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126251,
    "dDurationMs": 2419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "digital world was too great to \nsweep under the rug."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128670,
    "dDurationMs": 3086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Advertisers were already moving away\nfrom print and toward social"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131756,
    "dDurationMs": 1377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "media and digital media."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133133,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Consumers were cutting the cord\nand signing up for Netflix."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135844,
    "dDurationMs": 1376,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If this same advertiser"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137220,
    "dDurationMs": 1919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exodus was to happen with television,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139139,
    "dDurationMs": 2544,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then Disney and Fox\nwould both lose their golden geese."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141683,
    "dDurationMs": 4504,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Disney invested $400 million for 10% of VICE,\nthen offered to buy BuzzFeed for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146187,
    "dDurationMs": 1585,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "$650 million "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147772,
    "dDurationMs": 3462,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 2013 and then, when rejected,\noffered to buy VICE for $3.5"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151234,
    "dDurationMs": 2127,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "billion three years later."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153361,
    "dDurationMs": 918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet for the founders"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154279,
    "dDurationMs": 2627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of VICE and BuzzFeed,\ntheir calculus was simple. Why"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156906,
    "dDurationMs": 1377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sell for a couple hundred million "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158283,
    "dDurationMs": 3336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "today, when you could be a billionaire\ntycoon for the next generation?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161786,
    "dDurationMs": 1043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fast forward just 10"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162829,
    "dDurationMs": 2252,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years and BuzzFeed\ntoday is a penny stock."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165081,
    "dDurationMs": 2336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their viewership\nand readership are at record-lows"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167417,
    "dDurationMs": 1376,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "despite developing hit brands"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168793,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Tasty and breakthrough shows\nlike Hot Ones.  VICE"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171713,
    "dDurationMs": 2419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the other hand, declared \nbankruptcy in 2023."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174132,
    "dDurationMs": 3003,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They've both laid off staff\nand cut back on content, and the same has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177135,
    "dDurationMs": 2044,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been true for VOX and Business Insider."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179179,
    "dDurationMs": 2877,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many people have pointed the finger\nat mismanagement, greed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182056,
    "dDurationMs": 918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and venture capital."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182974,
    "dDurationMs": 4129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Former employees have all insisted that\nthese companies simply did too much, too fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187103,
    "dDurationMs": 2503,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the reality on closer\nlook is that no one else has been"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189606,
    "dDurationMs": 1418,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "able to figure out how to run a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191024,
    "dDurationMs": 2544,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sustainable media business\nwithout subscriptions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193568,
    "dDurationMs": 1918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You just can't give away all this content"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195486,
    "dDurationMs": 1168,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at scale for free."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196654,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While irresponsible\nspending accelerated their demise,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199365,
    "dDurationMs": 2878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "BuzzFeed and VICE at their core,\nare really more like driftwood."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202243,
    "dDurationMs": 1877,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were trapped in this volatile\nlandscape of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204120,
    "dDurationMs": 1376,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "online advertising and social"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205496,
    "dDurationMs": 2044,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "media, where they were initially beneficiaries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207540,
    "dDurationMs": 584,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but then soon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208124,
    "dDurationMs": 2586,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had the rug pulled out under them\nin many different ways."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210710,
    "dDurationMs": 4421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the end of the day, BuzzFeed, VICE, Vox,\nand Business Insider are not platforms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215131,
    "dDurationMs": 3921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're publications - no different\nfrom the Time Magazines, Reader's Digest,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219052,
    "dDurationMs": 917,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Men's Journal, or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219969,
    "dDurationMs": 1627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "People magazines that you saw as a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221596,
    "dDurationMs": 2544,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "kid at grocery stores\nor at doctor's offices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224140,
    "dDurationMs": 3629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Publishing has been a tough business even\nbefore the invention of the smartphone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227894,
    "dDurationMs": 834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While moving everything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228728,
    "dDurationMs": 3879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "online has eliminated certain costs\nand made access significant easier,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232607,
    "dDurationMs": 3462,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It still doesn't solve the costs\nof distribution and content creation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236110,
    "dDurationMs": 2461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not just the digital media startups\nthat are hurting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238571,
    "dDurationMs": 2044,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When we look at the rest of the\nlandscape, the legacy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240615,
    "dDurationMs": 1877,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "publishers are not faring any better."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242492,
    "dDurationMs": 2669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're not losing as much money\nas BuzzFeed, but they're also not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245161,
    "dDurationMs": 1085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doing any good business"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246246,
    "dDurationMs": 3003,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as their earnings and profits\nare all trending down year after year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249374,
    "dDurationMs": 2627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every leader is being forced\nto find answers and weather the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252001,
    "dDurationMs": 2503,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "storm, but there are only.\nSo many options available."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254504,
    "dDurationMs": 584,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They repeat the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255088,
    "dDurationMs": 3378,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same tactics at different times\nand still end up with the same results."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258466,
    "dDurationMs": 1919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When no one else has \nreally figured it out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260385,
    "dDurationMs": 1459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's not a single decision"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261844,
    "dDurationMs": 2336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where you can sit back and critique\nand say, BuzzFeed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264180,
    "dDurationMs": 2211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and VICE could have done this\nto save their business."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266391,
    "dDurationMs": 2878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The real question is, how could so many\nhit shows and millions of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269269,
    "dDurationMs": 1626,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "views be worth so little?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270895,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this episode, we're diving into BuzzFeed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272855,
    "dDurationMs": 3421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and analyzing the other players\nin the publishing landscape like People,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276276,
    "dDurationMs": 4337,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Business Insider, IGN,\nPCMag, and Time Magazine to understand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280613,
    "dDurationMs": 1251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where it all went wrong."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281864,
    "dDurationMs": 1627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What does the future hold in business?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283491,
    "dDurationMs": 2294,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As nine experts\nand you'll get ten answers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285785,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tune in to any news program\nand you'll see talking heads every day"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288705,
    "dDurationMs": 2210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "proclaiming\nthat a recession is just months away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290915,
    "dDurationMs": 3170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The tariffs will be eventually repealed,\nand that now is a good time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294085,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to buy the dip in American stocks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295795,
    "dDurationMs": 2085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Could someone please\ninvent a crystal ball?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297880,
    "dDurationMs": 3671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Until then, over 41,000 businesses\nhave future proofed their business"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301551,
    "dDurationMs": 1334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with NetSuite by Oracle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302885,
    "dDurationMs": 3838,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The number one cloud ERP\nbring accounting, finance, inventory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306723,
    "dDurationMs": 4254,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and HR into one fluid platform with one\nunified business management suite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311019,
    "dDurationMs": 2252,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's one source of truth\ngiving you the visibility"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313271,
    "dDurationMs": 2127,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and control\nyou need to make quick decisions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315398,
    "dDurationMs": 3211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With real time insights and forecasting,\nyou're peering into the future"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318609,
    "dDurationMs": 1168,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with actionable data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319777,
    "dDurationMs": 3003,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you're closing the books in days,\nnot weeks, you're spending less time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322780,
    "dDurationMs": 2503,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "looking backwards\nand more time on what's next."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325283,
    "dDurationMs": 1752,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Modern MBA is small at the moment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327035,
    "dDurationMs": 2794,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as soon as we scale,\nwe will need and used NetSuite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329829,
    "dDurationMs": 1585,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today we're stitching things manually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331414,
    "dDurationMs": 2210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's gotten harder\nto assess our business health."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333624,
    "dDurationMs": 3796,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We need to track production costs to run\npayroll compliant with multiple states,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337420,
    "dDurationMs": 2836,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and to evaluate profit\nand loss by team and project."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340256,
    "dDurationMs": 2211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a corporation,\nwe pay tax throughout the year"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342467,
    "dDurationMs": 3461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's a nightmare jumping from system\nto system just to get one answer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345970,
    "dDurationMs": 2336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are capabilities\nthat only NetSuite provides,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348306,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's a platform\nthat we intend to take every advantage of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351267,
    "dDurationMs": 3337,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whether your company is earning millions\nor even hundreds of millions, NetSuite"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354604,
    "dDurationMs": 3712,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "helps you respond to immediate challenges\nand seize your biggest opportunities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358358,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Speaking of opportunity, download the CFO's\nguide to AI and Machine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361778,
    "dDurationMs": 3295,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Learning at netsuite.com/ModernMBA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365073,
    "dDurationMs": 3169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The guide is free to you\nat NetSuite.com/ModernMBA"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368242,
    "dDurationMs": 3045,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "NetSuite.com/ModernMBA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372538,
    "dDurationMs": 1043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The rapid emergence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373581,
    "dDurationMs": 709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of BuzzFeed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374290,
    "dDurationMs": 3921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "VICE, Vox, and Business Insider through\nthe 2010s can be attributed to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378211,
    "dDurationMs": 1376,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "multiple paradigm shifts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379587,
    "dDurationMs": 3754,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As online-only publications, they were in\nthe best position to capitalize on them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383383,
    "dDurationMs": 583,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383966,
    "dDurationMs": 2795,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the evolution of Facebook\nas a distributor. In the 2000s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386761,
    "dDurationMs": 2294,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook had positioned itself\nas a social network,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389055,
    "dDurationMs": 250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389305,
    "dDurationMs": 2169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "main use-case was for people\nto stay up to date"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391474,
    "dDurationMs": 1376,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the people that they already knew."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392850,
    "dDurationMs": 1418,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The value of the platform was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394268,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dependent on their personal network."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395978,
    "dDurationMs": 1377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As Facebook opened up, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397355,
    "dDurationMs": 834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "userbase grew,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398189,
    "dDurationMs": 1293,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but homepages remain filled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399482,
    "dDurationMs": 2544,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with low-stakes status \nupdates and photo albums."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402026,
    "dDurationMs": 2795,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If Facebook was to grow as a business,\nit needed to improve its"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404821,
    "dDurationMs": 1251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "value to advertisers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406072,
    "dDurationMs": 1376,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the only way to do that was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407448,
    "dDurationMs": 1669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to increase user engagement."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409117,
    "dDurationMs": 625,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There needed to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409742,
    "dDurationMs": 2586,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something more dynamic, reoccurring,\nand interesting for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412328,
    "dDurationMs": 918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people to do beyond"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413246,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "waiting around for birthday\nreminders and life events."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415957,
    "dDurationMs": 1126,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the late 2000s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417083,
    "dDurationMs": 3879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the goalposts at Facebook had swung\nfrom account creation to session duration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420962,
    "dDurationMs": 3879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "People now needed to be spending\nas much time on facebook.com as possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424841,
    "dDurationMs": 1751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In terms of online recreation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426592,
    "dDurationMs": 2294,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their biggest rivals at the time\nwere the browser Flash games,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428886,
    "dDurationMs": 2378,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the cat videos of YouTube\nand the web"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431264,
    "dDurationMs": 2002,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "discovery websites like StumbleUpon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433266,
    "dDurationMs": 3378,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Zuckerberg was eager for engagement,\nbut also shrewd enough to let others"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436644,
    "dDurationMs": 2836,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do the work for him by following\nwhat Apple had done just a few"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439480,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years prior with the App Store on the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441190,
    "dDurationMs": 2253,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "iPhone. He generously opened up Facebook"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443443,
    "dDurationMs": 1876,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to developers in the late 2000s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445319,
    "dDurationMs": 3170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The most successful was Zynga,\nwho combined their exclusive access,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448489,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook's user data, and proven game\nmechanics to create Farmville."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451951,
    "dDurationMs": 1752,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Engagement exploded as users were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453703,
    "dDurationMs": 3170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "incentivized and prodded to visit Facebook\nmultiple times a day"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456873,
    "dDurationMs": 1918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to water their plants and feed animals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458791,
    "dDurationMs": 1335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Farmville was so successful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460126,
    "dDurationMs": 1251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that other developers copied"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461377,
    "dDurationMs": 2169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its formula, and the platform \nwas quickly swarmed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463546,
    "dDurationMs": 2794,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with copycat games\nthat all employed the same mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466340,
    "dDurationMs": 668,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even though people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467008,
    "dDurationMs": 2169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Were spending more time\nthan ever on the platform, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469177,
    "dDurationMs": 2002,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "engagement was happening inside the games."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471179,
    "dDurationMs": 2252,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most of the value was being captured\nby these outside"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473431,
    "dDurationMs": 1835,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "developers rather than Facebook."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475266,
    "dDurationMs": 2878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the same time, all these games ran \non Adobe Flash, which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478144,
    "dDurationMs": 1668,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was a poorly maintained proprietary"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479812,
    "dDurationMs": 2628,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "technology that had no future\non the mobile web."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482440,
    "dDurationMs": 1835,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second was user experience."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484275,
    "dDurationMs": 2211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was no secret that these games\ngot their adoption"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486486,
    "dDurationMs": 2544,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and engagement by spamming posts and notifications."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489030,
    "dDurationMs": 1418,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So while the games thrived, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490448,
    "dDurationMs": 3503,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "platform suffered as feeds\nbecame congested with automated spam."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493951,
    "dDurationMs": 2461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Without tools for good user-generated content,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496412,
    "dDurationMs": 2169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the only things left in people's\nFacebook feeds to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498581,
    "dDurationMs": 1084,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "look at were either copy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499665,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paste memes or external"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501125,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "links, but Facebook had got to where\nit was on the premise of quality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504545,
    "dDurationMs": 1961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There was a reputation\nthey had to uphold in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506506,
    "dDurationMs": 1001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ever-present race"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507507,
    "dDurationMs": 1501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "against Myspace and Twitter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509008,
    "dDurationMs": 3921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Turning the website into a social game\nportal and allowing user feeds to languish"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512929,
    "dDurationMs": 3628,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would only push away the quality users\nthat they had so carefully cultivated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516557,
    "dDurationMs": 1293,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the early 2010s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517850,
    "dDurationMs": 2044,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook had moved away from social games."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519894,
    "dDurationMs": 1335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They promised higher quality"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521229,
    "dDurationMs": 2877,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "useful, informative feeds for all\nand would directly push"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524106,
    "dDurationMs": 2294,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relevant external articles and \nvideos into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526400,
    "dDurationMs": 1210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every user's feeds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527610,
    "dDurationMs": 1793,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The evolution from social network to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529403,
    "dDurationMs": 2545,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "social media was now underway.\nLike they had done with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531948,
    "dDurationMs": 2377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "developers just a few years \nbefore, Facebook"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534325,
    "dDurationMs": 1168,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rolled out the red carpet to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535493,
    "dDurationMs": 3086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "publishers new and old from BuzzFeed\nto the New York Times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538621,
    "dDurationMs": 2419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook would now gladly\npush their content, even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541040,
    "dDurationMs": 2628,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as external links\nfor free to their global userbase"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543668,
    "dDurationMs": 1251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and these publications"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544919,
    "dDurationMs": 3629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could now even publish their articles\ndirectly on facebook.com by meeting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548548,
    "dDurationMs": 2669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consumers where they already were.\nPublishers, in theory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551217,
    "dDurationMs": 4171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would save on the costs of SEO, customer\nacquisition, and page optimization."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555513,
    "dDurationMs": 2085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was now no longer\nup to individuals to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557598,
    "dDurationMs": 2836,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "manually share articles one\nat a time on social media."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560434,
    "dDurationMs": 1335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook was now the willing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561769,
    "dDurationMs": 2085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and eager distributor for over a billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563854,
    "dDurationMs": 2878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people, with no way for any one \nuser to opt out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566732,
    "dDurationMs": 2837,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They had the best digital real estate,\nsecond only to Google"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569569,
    "dDurationMs": 2002,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the walled garden\nhad opened its doors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571571,
    "dDurationMs": 917,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was a marriage that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572488,
    "dDurationMs": 2377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "promised to solve problems for both sides."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574865,
    "dDurationMs": 3295,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook's problem was supply-side in\nnot having the quality content"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578160,
    "dDurationMs": 2294,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "needed to keep people on the site,\nand publishers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580454,
    "dDurationMs": 1168,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were struggling with demand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581622,
    "dDurationMs": 1752,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and getting more eyeballs on the content"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583374,
    "dDurationMs": 1501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they were already producing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584875,
    "dDurationMs": 2878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Zuckerberg pitched the big legacy \npublications, promising"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587753,
    "dDurationMs": 1961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "majority revenue share for their efforts and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589714,
    "dDurationMs": 3086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to build tools that would help them sell\ntheir existing subscription plans"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592800,
    "dDurationMs": 2377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "directly to users within his platform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595177,
    "dDurationMs": 751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He also wooed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595928,
    "dDurationMs": 3712,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "smaller publishers promising fair\nmerit-based distribution for all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599640,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook's algorithms would ensure\nthat the cream would rise to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602310,
    "dDurationMs": 3253,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the top. As long as enough\npeople shared, commented, and engaged,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605563,
    "dDurationMs": 1126,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then your piece of content"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606689,
    "dDurationMs": 2669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could go viral without ever\nneeding to pay for those views."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609358,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Any media was good media\nand all these publishers would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612069,
    "dDurationMs": 2336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "collectively make up for the absence of quality"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614405,
    "dDurationMs": 2211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "user-generated content on the platform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616616,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Interestingly enough,\nit would be the same over-reliance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619327,
    "dDurationMs": 2127,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on external content\nthat would give Snapchat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621454,
    "dDurationMs": 2586,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then eventually TikTok, the opening\nto surpass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624040,
    "dDurationMs": 542,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624582,
    "dDurationMs": 3378,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years later. BuzzFeed was the greatest\nbeneficiary of this change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627960,
    "dDurationMs": 1835,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They deviated from the norm by writing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629795,
    "dDurationMs": 3587,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Entertaining, casual content\nexclusively for this new social media."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633382,
    "dDurationMs": 1126,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "world in quizzes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634508,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "numbered lists, and articles\nthat had more pictures than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637178,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "text."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637678,
    "dDurationMs": 3921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All the content was, by design,\neasy to digest and even easier to share"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641641,
    "dDurationMs": 3169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thanks to the millions of free eyeballs\nthat Facebook was throwing their way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644852,
    "dDurationMs": 3837,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "BuzzFeed quickly established itself\nby the mid-2010s as the publication"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648689,
    "dDurationMs": 3879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for young adults, college students,\nand teenagers looking to kill time online."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652735,
    "dDurationMs": 2586,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the chickens soon came home to roost.\nIn the pursuit of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655321,
    "dDurationMs": 1293,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maximizing ad revenue,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656614,
    "dDurationMs": 2878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook had prioritized engagement\nabove all else, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659492,
    "dDurationMs": 2043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "marketers had studied its algorithms long"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661535,
    "dDurationMs": 876,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "enough to understand how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662411,
    "dDurationMs": 2378,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to engineer virality on the platform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664789,
    "dDurationMs": 1835,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Controversial and provocative content"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666624,
    "dDurationMs": 1835,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was rewarded for driving engagement"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668459,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and greater amounts of clickbait,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669919,
    "dDurationMs": 2502,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "misinformation, and fake news were pushed directly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672421,
    "dDurationMs": 4088,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to unsuspecting feeds. But to Facebook,\nany engagement was good engagement, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676509,
    "dDurationMs": 1001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the company turned a blind"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677510,
    "dDurationMs": 1793,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eye to keep the billions flowing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679303,
    "dDurationMs": 2294,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By 2016, Facebook was getting publicly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681597,
    "dDurationMs": 2044,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hammered for enabling the Cambridge\nAnalytica "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683641,
    "dDurationMs": 1001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scandal, allowing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684642,
    "dDurationMs": 2085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "foreign interference\nin multiple presidential"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686727,
    "dDurationMs": 2169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "elections, spreading misinformation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688896,
    "dDurationMs": 1752,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and being lax in moderation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690648,
    "dDurationMs": 1877,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the same year,\nwhere Zuckerberg was being"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 692525,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "criticized for not doing enough, \nBuzzFeed and VICE"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694985,
    "dDurationMs": 1836,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had reached their record valuations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696821,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "propelled by the seemingly\ninfinite streams of free social media"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700241,
    "dDurationMs": 2919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "traffic. Like every other publisher,\nthey never once imagined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703160,
    "dDurationMs": 2878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Facebook would actually\nturn off the golden spigot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706038,
    "dDurationMs": 2461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The scrutiny on Zuckerberg got\nso intense that the juice"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708499,
    "dDurationMs": 918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was no longer worth the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709417,
    "dDurationMs": 3253,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "squeeze. For the amount of reach\nand influence that Facebook now had,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712712,
    "dDurationMs": 291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they could"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713003,
    "dDurationMs": 1585,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no longer claim ignorance or shift"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714588,
    "dDurationMs": 1961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "responsibility back onto publishers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716549,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Suddenly, Facebook was publicly tasked\nwith the added responsibility"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719969,
    "dDurationMs": 2461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of moderating not just for safety but for truth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722430,
    "dDurationMs": 792,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which was a line that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723222,
    "dDurationMs": 1585,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "got blurred when juggled with demands"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724807,
    "dDurationMs": 3045,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from advertisers, brands, and \nvarious world governments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727935,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The cost of distributing media\nnow clearly outweighed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730646,
    "dDurationMs": 3378,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the benefits of user engagement.\nWith the strength of its subsidiaries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734024,
    "dDurationMs": 1335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in Instagram and WhatsApp,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735359,
    "dDurationMs": 2795,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook was also no longer as desperate \nfor engagement."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738154,
    "dDurationMs": 2043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The platform itself was fully mature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740197,
    "dDurationMs": 2503,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The younger generations\nhad shifted over to Instagram,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742700,
    "dDurationMs": 2836,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Snapchat, and TikTok, and publications\nhad no place in these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 745536,
    "dDurationMs": 2169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "short-form video and photo platforms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747705,
    "dDurationMs": 1918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The publishers were all now expendable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749623,
    "dDurationMs": 2419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Zuckerberg was free to pursue\nbigger dreams like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752042,
    "dDurationMs": 751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the metaverse"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752793,
    "dDurationMs": 2836,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in 2018, Facebook\nsuddenly turned off the spigot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755629,
    "dDurationMs": 459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They announced"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756088,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that all user feeds would now\nprioritize updates from friends rather"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759049,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than professional content\nfrom brands and publishers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761469,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This rugpull"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761969,
    "dDurationMs": 2336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "resulted in a direct drop in traffic\nfor every"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764305,
    "dDurationMs": 2127,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "publication as their biggest source of referral"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766432,
    "dDurationMs": 2502,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "behind Google seemingly evaporated overnight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768934,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Consumers now had to leave the platform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770644,
    "dDurationMs": 1877,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and seek out the content\nrather than wait to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772521,
    "dDurationMs": 1126,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "served it like beforea"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 773647,
    "dDurationMs": 751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this drop in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774398,
    "dDurationMs": 1502,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "traffic led to a decline in ad"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775900,
    "dDurationMs": 2294,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "revenue across the board for all publishers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778194,
    "dDurationMs": 2252,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The online-only digital media startups were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780446,
    "dDurationMs": 1752,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ultimately hit the hardest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782198,
    "dDurationMs": 1126,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The other paradigm shift"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783324,
    "dDurationMs": 1001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that gave digital media"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784325,
    "dDurationMs": 2919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "startups the rapid growth in the 2010s\nwas the inability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787244,
    "dDurationMs": 2878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of legacy publishers\nto evolve from print to digital."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790122,
    "dDurationMs": 2127,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There was never that much money\nin publishing even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792249,
    "dDurationMs": 2294,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before the smartphone and in the era of print."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794543,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can see that in the fundamentals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796003,
    "dDurationMs": 3837,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the prestigious name brand publications\nlike TIME Magazine, Entertainment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799840,
    "dDurationMs": 2628,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fortune, Sports Illustrated,\nand People Magazine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802468,
    "dDurationMs": 2085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of these publications\nhad been consolidated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804553,
    "dDurationMs": 3045,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "under one corporation,\nunder the goal of driving better margins"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807598,
    "dDurationMs": 1335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and greater deal sizes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808933,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With such diverse readership,\nthey would now be a one stop shop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811894,
    "dDurationMs": 2544,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for brands looking to hit a variety of demographics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814438,
    "dDurationMs": 2461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Time Warner's publishing division,\neven in its heyday"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816899,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before social media and smartphones"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 818609,
    "dDurationMs": 626,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had middling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819235,
    "dDurationMs": 2752,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "operating margins that were forever\nstuck in the teens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821987,
    "dDurationMs": 1293,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet in the same timeframe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823280,
    "dDurationMs": 918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the cable division"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824198,
    "dDurationMs": 2210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "enjoyed record profits year\nafter year, even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826408,
    "dDurationMs": 1127,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "though all of these magazines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827535,
    "dDurationMs": 2043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "charged readers upfront for access."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829578,
    "dDurationMs": 1752,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The reality is that they still made most"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831330,
    "dDurationMs": 2794,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their money through advertising\nrather than subscriptions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834124,
    "dDurationMs": 4088,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when the iPhone was introduced in\n2007, Time Warner's publishing business"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838212,
    "dDurationMs": 2377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "began to falter and has since never recovered."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840589,
    "dDurationMs": 876,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their leaders believed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841465,
    "dDurationMs": 1001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that all they had to do in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842466,
    "dDurationMs": 3087,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this new age was to simply offer\nthe same subscriptions online."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845553,
    "dDurationMs": 2752,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their assumption was that readers, brands, \nand advertisers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848305,
    "dDurationMs": 3921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would repeat the same patterns online as\nthey had done offline for so many decades."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852226,
    "dDurationMs": 2836,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They expected competition but \nnever imagined that their challengers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 855062,
    "dDurationMs": 2252,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be giving away\nso much content for free,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857314,
    "dDurationMs": 3045,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially at the quality\nand volume of BuzzFeed and VICE."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860401,
    "dDurationMs": 2419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of these digital media startups\nhad placed their chips"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862820,
    "dDurationMs": 2294,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on a fundamentally different \nbusiness model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865114,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their collective belief\nwas that they could be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866824,
    "dDurationMs": 2044,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profitable off advertising alone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 868868,
    "dDurationMs": 2210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The rationale was that \nwithout the costs of physical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 871078,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "delivery and printing presses,\nthey would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873038,
    "dDurationMs": 2002,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "never need to charge for subscriptions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875040,
    "dDurationMs": 2336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since ad revenue\nis a function of eyeballs,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 877376,
    "dDurationMs": 2127,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if they were to block access\nbased on payment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879503,
    "dDurationMs": 2252,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or registration, that would \nonly reduce the number of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881755,
    "dDurationMs": 2378,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eyeballs and the amount of dollars\nin the long run."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884133,
    "dDurationMs": 792,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, while Time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884925,
    "dDurationMs": 2378,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Warner continued to push memberships\nin print into the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887303,
    "dDurationMs": 1126,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2010s to maintain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888429,
    "dDurationMs": 3086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their older audience, these startups\nflourished in the same period,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891515,
    "dDurationMs": 3462,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "filling the void that was left behind\nby the legacy publications with their"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894977,
    "dDurationMs": 1126,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "free content."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896103,
    "dDurationMs": 1919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While subscription has remained\nfairly resilient"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898022,
    "dDurationMs": 3336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the legacy publications,\ntheir biggest impact was in ad revenue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901400,
    "dDurationMs": 3086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Running a single page ad in the Time\nMagazine would cost hundreds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 904486,
    "dDurationMs": 2753,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of thousands of dollars\nalone in placement. In comparison,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 907239,
    "dDurationMs": 1585,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anyone could make a Facebook ad in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908824,
    "dDurationMs": 2252,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "minutes for as low as $1 a day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911076,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brands and marketers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912036,
    "dDurationMs": 3753,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flocked to social media, which offered\nradically cheaper ads, self-service"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 915789,
    "dDurationMs": 2837,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "options, measurable impact\nand precise targeting all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 918626,
    "dDurationMs": 834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out of the box"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 919460,
    "dDurationMs": 3336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without the baggage and bureaucracy\nof the print publications. BuzzFeed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922796,
    "dDurationMs": 3087,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "VICE and the other startups were able\nto build the tools and analytics that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925883,
    "dDurationMs": 459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the brands and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926342,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "agencies were looking for\nin this new online"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928802,
    "dDurationMs": 2461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "frontier. Yet television remained impervious to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931263,
    "dDurationMs": 2586,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these changes.  While the publishing business regressed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933849,
    "dDurationMs": 1293,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Time Warner's cable division"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 935142,
    "dDurationMs": 2085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "continued to grow to record earnings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937227,
    "dDurationMs": 2586,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the early 2010s,\nthe once reliable publishing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939813,
    "dDurationMs": 2336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "division had become such a liability\nthat the company"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 942149,
    "dDurationMs": 1627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leaders were ready to abandon it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 943776,
    "dDurationMs": 1585,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its profits were lower than even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 945361,
    "dDurationMs": 2419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that of the Hollywood motion\npicture business."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947780,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To get rid of the deadwood, Time Warner"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949740,
    "dDurationMs": 3128,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spun out its publishing division\nas its own independent entity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952868,
    "dDurationMs": 1251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where in theory - it could be more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954119,
    "dDurationMs": 2253,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "agile and focused on turning things around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956372,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But despite their best efforts\nto match BuzzFeed's throughput"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959083,
    "dDurationMs": 3461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and to cut costs down to the bone,\nthe now independent Time Magazine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 962544,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still could not stop the drop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964254,
    "dDurationMs": 2712,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Operating margins plummeted \nyear after year to record low"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966966,
    "dDurationMs": 2335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "single digits and eventually turned negative."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 969301,
    "dDurationMs": 2378,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ironically, it was the income from subscriptions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 971679,
    "dDurationMs": 2669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that kept the company's lights\non for as long as they did."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974348,
    "dDurationMs": 1585,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If they were somehow an advertising"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 975933,
    "dDurationMs": 1835,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only business without subscriptions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977768,
    "dDurationMs": 1376,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "TIME Magazine would have only lost"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979144,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "greater amounts of money\nat a much earlier stage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 981855,
    "dDurationMs": 2128,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only independent publisher operating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983983,
    "dDurationMs": 3128,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at scale in this day and age\nthat's not part of some massive media"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987111,
    "dDurationMs": 1918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "conglomerate and\nwhose profit margins are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989029,
    "dDurationMs": 2544,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually increasing and not\ndecreasing year over year"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 991573,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the New York Times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993033,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They've achieved that\nby shifting their business"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 994743,
    "dDurationMs": 3671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from being advertising-centric to\nsubscription-centric, and that income has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998414,
    "dDurationMs": 2335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "enabled them to thrive\nin periods of downturn."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000749,
    "dDurationMs": 1335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The ad market at its"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1002084,
    "dDurationMs": 459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "core is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1002543,
    "dDurationMs": 4212,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "seasonal and cyclical, and the deal sizes,\nflow and interest will always be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006755,
    "dDurationMs": 2544,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out of the hands of the publishers\nand content creators."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1009299,
    "dDurationMs": 2169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Subscriptions serve as an invaluable hedge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011468,
    "dDurationMs": 2836,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and provide reoccurring, stable, upfront revenue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1014304,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the company gets compensated\nto deliver content."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016974,
    "dDurationMs": 2085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In contrast, BuzzFeed, VICE, and digital"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019059,
    "dDurationMs": 1669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "media startups all thumbed their nose"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020728,
    "dDurationMs": 2544,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at subscriptions as outdated, unnecessary,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023272,
    "dDurationMs": 2669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "predatory monetization\ntactics of the past."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1025941,
    "dDurationMs": 2795,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They simply created content and\nassumed that there would be sufficient"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028736,
    "dDurationMs": 2669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "monetization opportunities after delivery."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1031405,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ultimately, if you want to survive as an online"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1033365,
    "dDurationMs": 2252,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "publisher or content creator,\nthere are really"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035617,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only two proven options."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1037077,
    "dDurationMs": 1043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You either stay small"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038120,
    "dDurationMs": 2502,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like most influencers\nor you charge subscriptions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040622,
    "dDurationMs": 2962,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on top of advertisements.\nAdvertising with or without"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043584,
    "dDurationMs": 3003,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook's free traffic\nwill simply never be enough at scale"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1046587,
    "dDurationMs": 1334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as we'll soon see later with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047921,
    "dDurationMs": 2086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "BuzzFeed's business post-IPO."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1050007,
    "dDurationMs": 2127,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ironically, the New York Times was criticized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052134,
    "dDurationMs": 3503,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through the 2010s for clinging onto\nsubscriptions and paywall their content,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1055637,
    "dDurationMs": 1252,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as it stands today"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1056889,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "10 years later, they had been right the entire time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1059850,
    "dDurationMs": 1585,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The third and final paradigm shift"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1061435,
    "dDurationMs": 2669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through the 2010s that allowed BuzzFeed and \nother digital"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064104,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "media startups to flourish\nwas the shift to video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066774,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The cable networks historically \nhad been the gatekeepers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069234,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for video for consumers and publishers alike."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071904,
    "dDurationMs": 1001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Consumers needed to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1072905,
    "dDurationMs": 4045,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "buy cable or DVDs to access video,\nand publishers were dependent on the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1076950,
    "dDurationMs": 2086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cable networks to distribute their content."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1079036,
    "dDurationMs": 2878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As smartphone adoption and\nCellular technology matured, it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1081914,
    "dDurationMs": 2043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now became possible\nto watch high resolution"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083957,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "videos on the go through the internet\nand for the publishers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086627,
    "dDurationMs": 3211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to bypass the cable companies\nand to stream their content directly to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1089838,
    "dDurationMs": 2044,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Users. Video as a format was more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1091882,
    "dDurationMs": 1126,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "engaging than text, but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1093008,
    "dDurationMs": 1418,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more importantly, it was a much"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094426,
    "dDurationMs": 2044,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "better form of mobile advertising."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1096470,
    "dDurationMs": 2085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While the shift from print to digital.\nmeant brands"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1098555,
    "dDurationMs": 584,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could now measure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099139,
    "dDurationMs": 3253,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exactly how many people were seeing\nor clicking into their ads, the mobile"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1102392,
    "dDurationMs": 2128,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Internet brought new challenges.\nSince the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1104520,
    "dDurationMs": 1167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dawn of the World Wide Web,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105687,
    "dDurationMs": 1168,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "online ads had been"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106855,
    "dDurationMs": 3671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "squeezed around or often in front of\ncontent in the form of banners and pop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110526,
    "dDurationMs": 1501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ups, but the average smartphone"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112027,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "screen was 75%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1113487,
    "dDurationMs": 3295,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "smaller, or a quarter of the size\nof the average desktop monitor,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116782,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with only a quarter of the screen\nreal estate for mobile users."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119743,
    "dDurationMs": 918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There was very little,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1120661,
    "dDurationMs": 3545,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if any, white space left to squeeze\nin banner ads and pop-ups like before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1124331,
    "dDurationMs": 1210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, video became the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1125541,
    "dDurationMs": 1501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "superior medium for serving"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1127042,
    "dDurationMs": 2878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mobile ads as the advertisement\nwould fill the entire screen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1129920,
    "dDurationMs": 1835,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "during playback and it couldn't be skipped,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1131755,
    "dDurationMs": 2378,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thereby guaranteeing brands full impressions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134133,
    "dDurationMs": 1918,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since all ads are fundamentally"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1136051,
    "dDurationMs": 2336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "charged by the number of impressions,\nevery brand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138387,
    "dDurationMs": 625,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "naturally wanted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1139012,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make sure that they were paying\nfor real eyeballs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1141723,
    "dDurationMs": 835,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every publisher"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142558,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "saw the same opportunity to create videos\nthat could fill this content gap"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1145978,
    "dDurationMs": 1668,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between cable TV and the low"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1147646,
    "dDurationMs": 1335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "effort memes on YouTube."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1148981,
    "dDurationMs": 2836,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was a gold rush,\nbut there was real gold to be had here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1151817,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For decades, the cable networks\nwere like the video cartel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1154528,
    "dDurationMs": 1543,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They had amassed massive fortunes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1156071,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being exclusive distributors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1157781,
    "dDurationMs": 1919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If publishers could reclaim\njust a fraction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159700,
    "dDurationMs": 2002,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of that television\nad spend for themselves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1161702,
    "dDurationMs": 2127,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it would still be worth\nbillions of dollars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1163829,
    "dDurationMs": 2586,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This all played out in 2016,\njust 2 years before"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1166415,
    "dDurationMs": 2335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook would yank\nthe rug from beneath the feet of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1168750,
    "dDurationMs": 2002,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "publishers. Zuckerberg publicly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1170752,
    "dDurationMs": 751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fanned the flames,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171503,
    "dDurationMs": 1543,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "boasting that the world was entering a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1173046,
    "dDurationMs": 3045,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "golden age of video based on all\nthe big data they had at their"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1176091,
    "dDurationMs": 667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fingertips."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1176758,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He predicted that in five years time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1178468,
    "dDurationMs": 2336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people would no longer be reading\nmost of their content,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1180804,
    "dDurationMs": 1794,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but instead watching it. Text"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1182598,
    "dDurationMs": 1376,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be a thing of the past."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1183974,
    "dDurationMs": 2336,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Based on all the free traffic\nthey were getting from Facebook,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1186310,
    "dDurationMs": 1418,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every publisher from BuzzFeed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1187728,
    "dDurationMs": 4045,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the New York Times, had no reason\nto doubt Zuckerberg. With his confirmation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1191773,
    "dDurationMs": 668,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they aggressively"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1192441,
    "dDurationMs": 2794,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chased video, invested in production teams, \nlaid off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1195235,
    "dDurationMs": 1919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "writers, and built in-house studios."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1197154,
    "dDurationMs": 2586,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But their misstep\nwas more technical than creative."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1199740,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What the legacy publications got wrong\nwas that they all unanimously refused"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1203660,
    "dDurationMs": 1085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to embrace YouTube."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1204745,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They instead"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1205245,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "focused their efforts on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1206205,
    "dDurationMs": 2794,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hosting the videos themselves,\nunder the crazy belief that they could"
